{#-
  === Macro Module: Narrative Contract Rendering ===
  File Type: Macro Module
  Brief Description: Renders the narrative_contract object into a markdown-formatted narrative contract paragraph, containing world rules, tone constraints, themes, character arcs, ending strategies, continuity protocols, and other information.

  Defined Macros and Parameters:
  1. render_narrative_contract(narrative_contract, mode: str = "chapter")
     - mode optional values: "chapter" (default) | "plan" | "bridge" | "draft"
     - Different modes determine which fields are displayed (e.g., plan mode shows character arcs, draft mode shows information density budget, etc.)

  Usage:
  - Called by templates such as planning/plan_chapter.j2, writing/draft_chapter.j2, writing/bridge_chapter.j2 via {% import %}
-#}
{% macro render_narrative_contract(narrative_contract, mode="chapter") -%}
{% if narrative_contract %}
{% set _suffix = " — Must be followed during planning" if mode == "plan" else (" — Must be followed for all chapter bridges" if mode == "bridge" else "") %}
## Global Narrative Contract (★ Hard Constraint{{ _suffix }})
{% if narrative_contract.world_rules %}- World Rules: {{ narrative_contract.world_rules | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if narrative_contract.tone %}- Tone Constraints: {{ narrative_contract.tone }}{% endif %}
{% set _wc = narrative_contract.world_context %}
{% if _wc %}
- Era Context/Ritual Constraints (executed as world rules during writing):
{% if _wc.social_hierarchy %}  - Social Hierarchy: {{ _wc.social_hierarchy }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.address_rules %}  - Address/Title Rules: {{ _wc.address_rules | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.self_reference_rules %}  - Self-Reference Rules: {{ _wc.self_reference_rules | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.etiquette_rules %}  - Ritual/Behavioral Boundaries: {{ _wc.etiquette_rules | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.institution_terms %}  - Institutional Terminology: {{ _wc.institution_terms | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.material_culture %}  - Era Artifacts: {{ _wc.material_culture | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.anachronism_blacklist %}  - Anachronism Blacklist: {{ _wc.anachronism_blacklist | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if _wc.dialogue_register_rules %}  - Dialogue Register: {{ _wc.dialogue_register_rules | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if mode in ["plan", "bridge"] and narrative_contract.themes %}- Core Themes: {{ narrative_contract.themes | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% if mode == "plan" and narrative_contract.character_arcs %}
- Character Arcs:
{% for arc in narrative_contract.character_arcs %}
  - {{ arc.name }} ({{ arc.role }}): {{ arc.arc }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if narrative_contract.ending_strategy %}- Ending Trajectory{% if mode == "draft" %} (note the direction of setup during writing){% endif %}: {{ narrative_contract.ending_strategy }}{% endif %}
{% if mode == "plan" and narrative_contract.key_turning_points %}- Key Turning Points: {{ narrative_contract.key_turning_points | join('; ') }}{% endif %}
{% set _cp = narrative_contract.continuity_protocol %}
{% if _cp %}
  - Continuity Protocol (initialization hard rules):
  - Scene Transition: When the opening location changes, the first {{ story_bible.get('location_transition_window_sentences', 3) }} sentences must contain a movement action chain.
  - Bridge Landing: The first {{ story_bible.get('bridge_echo_window_chars', 900) }} characters before the opening must respond to {{ "action_handoff" if mode == "bridge" else "bridge.action_handover" }}.
  - Time Legitimacy: {{ time_convention | default('Naturally select time units according to the project era background') }}
  - POV Visibility: {{ _cp.pov_visibility_rule | default('Limited POV only describes observable facts.') }}
  - Forbidden Repetition Rule: {{ _cp.forbidden_repetition_rule | default('Forbidden elements must not be paraphrased.') }}
{% if mode == "plan" %}
  - Information Density Budget (★ Hard Constraint): No more than {{ story_bible.get('max_key_revelations_per_chapter', 2) }} major revelations per chapter; excess must be changed to foreshadowing or misleading clues.
{% elif mode == "draft" %}
  - Information Density Budget (★ Hard Constraint): No more than {{ story_bible.get('max_key_revelations_per_chapter', 2) }} major revelations per chapter.
{% endif %}
{% if mode in ["plan", "draft"] %}
  - Suspense Preservation: This chapter must retain at least {{ story_bible.get('min_unresolved_threads_to_keep', 1) }} unresolved thread(s) entering the next chapter (if 0, not enforced).
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}